<div class="bio">
  <figure class="bio-map"><!--#inc fig-journey.svg --><figcaption>His route, from his own biography. The cities sit at their real relative positions.<sup class="s"><a href="#s9">9</a></sup></figcaption></figure>
  <ol class="journey">
    <li><span class="jy">Lisbon</span><b>Born in Lisbon</b><span>He found music early, studying at the Instituto Gregoriano de Lisboa.</span></li>
    <li><span class="jy">Mid-1980s</span><b>The Algarve</b><span>His family moved south, and he began formal lessons in guitar and composition. Later, as Dinis tells it, a band with his brother on drums: about twelve gigs a week.<sup class="s"><a href="#s1">1</a></sup></span></li>
    <li><span class="jy">Mid-1990s</span><b>London</b><span>Advanced studies: the Musicians Institute, a BTEC in Popular Music at City and Islington College, then a BMus (Hons) in Composition at the London College of Music.</span></li>
    <li><span class="jy">A career</span><b>Concert, film, television, radio, new media</b><span>"A versatile career as a composer, working across a wide range of genres and mediums."</span></li>
    <li class="now"><span class="jy">The last decade</span><b>Additional music on Hollywood productions</b><span>An Additional Music Composer on major Hollywood film productions, in his words. His own site leads with three: The Bay, War Flowers and The Gauntlet.</span></li>
  </ol>
</div>
<p class="scnote">From the biography on his own site, gabrieldacruz.com, read 18 November 2026; the quotes are his.<sup class="s"><a href="#s9">9</a></sup> The band is his brother's account.</p>
